"CSS Properties and Values API Level 1 (https://drafts.css-houdini.org/css-properties-values-api-1/)\nciteturn1279view0 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: find({\"ref_id\":\"https://drafts.css-houdini.org/css-properties-values-api-1/\",\"pattern\":\"canonical\"}); Total lines: 1339\nL148:   * If the specified value is a cite99†dimension†drafts.csswg.org literal (such as 50em or .2s), the computed value is the same value, but with the unit converted to the corresponding cite100†canonical unit†drafts.csswg.org for the type of value.\nL149: \nL150:   * If the specified value is any other numeric literal (such as 5 or 20%), the computed value is as specified. (In particular, percentages are never resolved against anything.)\nL151:   * If the specified value is a function that evaluates to one of those types (such as a cite101†math function†drafts.csswg.org ), the computed value is defined by that function.\nL152: \nL153: For `\"<string>\"` values, the computed value is as specified.\nL154: \nL155: For `\"<color>\"` values, the value is computed by resolving color values, per cite102†CSS Color 4 §  15. Resolving <color> Values†drafts.csswg.org .\nL156: \nL157: For `\"<custom-ident>\"`, ident, or `\"*\"` values, the computed value is as specified.\nL951:     * reconsume the current input code point\nL952:     * starts with an ident sequence\nL953:     * whitespace\nL954:   * [CSS-TRANSFORMS-1] defines the following terms:\nL955:     * <transform-function>\nL956:     * <transform-list>\nL957:     * transform\nL958:   * [CSS-TYPED-OM-1] defines the following terms:\nL959:     * CSSStyleValue\nL960:     * [[associatedProperty]]\nL961:     * custom property name string\nL962:     * reify a <transform-function>\nL963:     * reify a <transform-list>\nL964:     * reify a list of component values\nL965:     * reify a numeric value\nL966:     * reify an identifier\nL967:     * reify as a CSSStyleValue\nL968:   * [CSS-VALUES-4] defines th